    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the number of different starting lineups possible, we need to consider that two specific players, Ace and Zeppo, are already guaranteed to be in the lineup. This means we only need to choose the remaining 3 players from the other 10 players on the team.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 3 players from 10 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{r} = \\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of players to choose from, \\( r \\) is the number of players to choose, and \\( ! \\) denotes factorial. Here, \\( n = 10 \\) and \\( r = 3 \\).\n\nSo, we calculate \\( \\binom{10}{3} \\) as follows:\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{3! \\times 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{720}{6} = 120\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting lineups possible is \\(\\boxed{120}\\).",
